      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Critics often claim wealth taxes will destroy capital investment and cause mass emigration, but history shows that moderate taxes on the ultra-wealthy actually stimulate innovation by leveling the playing field for small businesses. They also argue it's politically impossible to pass, yet this is a political failure of our current system, not an economic flaw, as we have successfully passed other progressive measures like the Affordable Care Act. The real danger of inequality isn't just economic stagnation; it's the social fragmentation and political instability that wealth concentration inevitably breeds. You should focus your paper on how wealth taxes can be structured to target the top 1% without harming small business owners, proving that the \"myths\" are just fear-mongering from those who benefit from the status quo.",
      "source": "target",
