      "content": "i hear you on the enforcement part, but isn't it a bit dangerous to dismiss the \"economic collapse\" argument as just a myth when so many economists are genuinely worried? even if the administrative side is solvable, many argue that the constant uncertainty and the loss of domestic capital fundamentally change how markets function. wouldn't a truly neutral analysis have to admit that these risks aren't just \"fear-mongering,\" but are legitimate, evidence-based concerns that could actually happen?",
